{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Consensus Decision-Making in Design.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Consensus Decision-Making in Design.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"consensus decision making in design consensus decision making in design","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Consensus Decision-Making in Design.md","fileName":"Consensus Decision-Making in Design.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Consensus Decision-Making in Design","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 00:27\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Collaborative Game Development]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Collaborative Game Development","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Consensus Decision-Making in Design.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Consensus Decision-Making in Design.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"consensus decision making in design consensus decision making in design","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Consensus Decision-Making in Design.md","fileName":"Consensus Decision-Making in Design.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Consensus Decision-Making in Design","heading":"Consensus Decision-Making in Design","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Consensus decision-making seeks a proposal every affected collaborator can support or accept, even if it is not each person's first choice. It differs from unanimity of preference and from majority rule that leaves a persistent minority unheard.\n\nThe method works best when the team has shared design values and a defined way to end discussion. Evidence from a prototype can transform an abstract dispute into a question the group can observe together.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Collaborative Game Development","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - F